." GPRename manual page
.TH GPRENAME 1 "2026-08-17" "GPRename 2026.08" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gprename \- graphical batch renamer for files and directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gprename
.RI [ PATH ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
GPRename is a graphical batch renamer for files and directories.  It provides
case conversion, insertion and deletion, replacement with optional regular
expressions, and sequential numeric renaming.
.PP
This release is a native Python 3 / GTK 4 rewrite of the historical Perl/Gtk3
implementation.  It does not load Gtk3.pm or any Perl modules.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I PATH
Open the specified directory.  If a regular file is supplied, its containing
directory is opened.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/gprename/gprename
User settings, or the file below
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
when that environment variable is set.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gprename/gprename_log
Rename and undo log.
.SH NOTES
The safe rename implementation stages selected entries through unique
temporary names.  This permits case-only changes and rename cycles without
clobbering unrelated files.
.SH AUTHOR
GPRename contributors.
